## Dash camera
cmu-dash-camera-already = {CAPITALIZE(THE($vehicle))} already has a dash camera.
cmu-dash-camera-fitting = You start fitting the dash camera to {THE($vehicle)}.
cmu-dash-camera-fitted = You fit the dash camera to {THE($vehicle)}. It's streaming to the CMB monitors.
cmu-dash-camera-name = Dashcam: {$vehicle}
cmu-dash-camera-examine = Use it on a vehicle to fit it.
cmu-dash-camera-examine-shorted = Its electronics are fried. It won't stream again until it's taken off and refitted.
cmu-dash-camera-examine-vehicle = A [color=red]dash camera[/color] is fitted, streaming to the CMB monitors. A screwdriver and a law enforcement ID will take it off.
cmu-dash-camera-examine-vehicle-shorted = A [color=red]dash camera[/color] is fitted, but its electronics are fried. A screwdriver will take it off.
cmu-dash-camera-no-id = The dash camera's mount is locked. You need a CMB, CWPS or NSPA ID to unscrew it, or you could short it out with a multitool.
cmu-dash-camera-unscrewing = You start unscrewing the dash camera from {THE($vehicle)}.
cmu-dash-camera-removed = You take the dash camera off {THE($vehicle)}.
cmu-dash-camera-already-shorted = The dash camera is already fried.
cmu-dash-camera-shorting = You start shorting out the dash camera's electronics.
cmu-dash-camera-shorted = The dash camera sparks and its light goes dark. It's no longer streaming.
